# Compound components

New components that have layout variants use a compound shape. The root owns shared state and provides it to parts. Parts read that context and fail with a clear error outside the root. Consumers compose with children (`Component.Part`), not with boolean or slot props. Do not duplicate the root's state in a part. Keep the context private to the folder. Prefer one file until it is hard to navigate, then split parts inside the same folder without exporting the context.
